  "x-speechnexus-text-stream": {
    "unit": "Unicode scalar values (codepoints), never UTF-8 bytes or UTF-16 code units; unpaired surrogates are invalid.",
    "invariants": [
      "Submit command must be tts with text_stream matching open stream_id/epoch. Open/opened input_kind must match; PCM input is forbidden in text mode. A stream epoch is never reused.",
      "Before opened no append/commit/finish is accepted. text_seq starts at 0 and is contiguous over append/commit/finish per epoch. Only one unacknowledged sender event is in flight.",
      "Append offset_codepoints equals accepted_through_codepoint; accepted length may not exceed absolute credit_through_codepoint. Open credit initializes this absolute limit; each ack grants a monotonic absolute limit, not an additive amount.",
      "An exact retry of a previously accepted text_seq returns its original ack without regenerating text; changed kind/body at that sequence is text_conflict. Future sequence is text_gap. Store canonical event digest and ack through execution retention.",
      "Commit through_codepoint lies between prior committed and accepted offsets. Only immutable committed prefix reaches the adapter. Repeating a commit cannot schedule the prefix twice.",
      "Finish final_codepoint equals accepted offset and commits its remaining suffix once. Finished ack is required; subsequent new append/commit/finish is text_finished. Exact retries still return their original ack.",
      "Ack satisfies committed <= accepted <= credit. Latest accepted text_seq/offsets/credit never decrease; an original ack replay for an older text_seq must not replace later high-water state. -1 means no accepted text event yet. Credit exceeding max_message_bytes is not permission to send an oversized frame.",
      "Cancel/disconnect does not imply termination or release. New epoch resumes no unacknowledged text; query the original execution, abort or reconcile before creating a replacement. stream.closed follows verified execution and cleanup facts."
    ]
  }
